q_select_context.1:
Decide how much of this opened node the NEXT decisions about the UNIT need to see:
0 drop: irrelevant to the unit;
1 handle: only its one-line claim matters;
2 summary: its summary matters, not its body;
3 full: its body matters (the unit may restate, answer, close, contradict or supersede it).

q_classify_disposition.1:
Classify how the UNIT should be disposed of on the board:
- new_content: it states something the board does not yet hold and that deserves its own node (a directive, decision, constraint, problem, question, idea, risk, milestone or note);
- authorizes_work: it authorizes or asks for work to be done (a task, a round of work, an investigation);
- context_only: it is conversational or background context that changes nothing on the board (acknowledgements, commands such as /compact, thinking aloud);
- duplicate_of_existing: an existing node already says it.

q_proposal_disposition.1:
A worker's report PROPOSES a node write (the UNIT). Decide how the fold-after pass disposes of the proposal:
- accept_new: accept it as a new node;
- accept_as_update_of_existing: it is really an update of an existing node (its own id, or the matched node): apply it there;
- duplicate_drop: an existing node already says it; drop it;
- reject_out_of_scope: it does not belong on this workspace's board.

